   {:added "1.0"})
 
+(add-doc-and-meta *read-positions*
+  "When set to logical true, reading from a LineNumberingPushbackReader
+  (as load, load-file and the REPL do) attaches :line and :column
+  metadata to non-empty vector, map and set literals, as it always does
+  for lists, and :file when *file* names the file being loaded. The
+  compiler keeps literal metadata on the values those literals evaluate
+  to, so data built from code can tell where in the source it was
+  written. Intended for development tooling.
+
+  Defaults to false, or to the system property 'clojure.read.positions':
+
+  java -Dclojure.read.positions=true ..."
+  {:added "1.13"})
+
 (add-doc-and-meta *assert*
   "When set to logical false, 'assert' will omit assertion checks in
   compiled code. Defaults to true."
